{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-033db329", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Background determined from MC simulation only (no dedicated data-driven normalisation)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 36 analyses that estimate a background using methods that are based on MC simulation only (no dedicated data-driven normalisation). These methods include:\n\n- Direct MC simulation estimate (no control-region normalisation)\n- Direct simulation-based background estimate (fixed normalization, no CR fit)\n- Background fixed to SM MC prediction with assigned normalisation uncertainty\n\nThese methods are used across various backgrounds such as $Z/\\\\gamma^{*}+\\\\mathrm{jets}$, $WZ$, $WW$, $VVV$, and others.\n\nTo provide a more detailed breakdown, the following papers are among those that use these methods:\n\n- **2004.14060**: $Z\\\\to\\\\nu\\\\bar{\\\\nu}$ + heavy-flavour jets background\n- **2007.02873**: Z+jets background\n- **2010.14293**: Z+jets background (Z→νν)\n- **2012.03799**: Z+jets background\n- **2102.01444**: $Wt$ single-top background, $Z/\\\\gamma^{*}+\\\\mathrm{jets}$ background, and \"Others\" minor background category\n- **2106.01676**: SM WZ background, Z+jets (FNP-lepton) background\n- **2109.13808**: Drell-Yan Z/gamma*+jets background, Non-resonant WW diboson background\n- **2110.11231**: VVV triboson background\n- **2202.08676**: WZ irreducible background\n- **2208.12095**: $Z{+}\\\\text{jets}$ background\n- **2211.08028**: Z+jets background\n- **2308.02285**: Diboson (WW, WZ, ZZ) background, Z+jets (or virtual photon) background\n- **2312.04450**: $Z$+jets background, $WZ$+jets background, $ZZ$+jets background, $tWZ$ background\n- **2401.05299**: $VV$ (diboson) background\n- **2503.19420**: $WZ$ background, $VVV$ background, $Z\\\\textrm{+jets}$ background\n\nThis list is not exhaustive, but it provides a representative sample of the analyses that use these methods. \n\nIf you need more specific details or a different breakdown, please let me know.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The graph records 36 analyses that estimate a background using methods that are based on MC simulation only (no dedicated data-driven normalisation). These methods include direct MC simulation estimates, direct simulation-based background estimates, and background fixed to SM MC predictions with assigned normalisation uncertainties. Some of the papers that use these methods are 2004.14060, 2007.02873, 2010.14293, 2012.03799, 2102.01444, 2106.01676, 2109.13808, 2110.11231, 2202.08676, 2208.12095, 2211.08028, 230", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.12246", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2407.10549", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2604.27044", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Background determined from MC simulation only (no dedicated data-driven normalisation)"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.657}, {"round": 2, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "background_uses_method", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 152, "error": null, "seconds": 0.043}, {"round": 3, "tool": "describe", "args": {"entity_ids": ["hepkg:background:others-minor", "hepkg:background:diboson-vv", "hepkg:background