{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-04a5d234", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define the object Lepton (electron or muon)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses define the object \"Lepton (electron or muon)\":\n\n1. **$CP$ Properties of Higgs Boson Interactions with Top Quarks in the $t\\bar{t}H$ and $tH$ Processes Using $H\\rightarrow\\gamma\\gamma$ with the ATLAS Detector** (arXiv: 2004.04545)\n2. **Constraints on Higgs boson properties using $WW^{*}(→ eνμν)jj$ production in 36.1 fb⁻¹ of $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV $pp$ collisions with the ATLAS detector** (arXiv: 2109.13808)\n3. **Constraints on Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum using $H\\rightarrow b\\bar{b}$ decays in the ATLAS detector** (arXiv: 2111.08340)\n4. **Combination and interpretation of differential Higgs boson production cross sections in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV** (arXiv: 2504.13081)\n5. **Combination of searches for nonresonant Higgs boson pair production in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV** (arXiv: 2510.07527)\n6. **Constraints on anomalous Higgs boson couplings to vector bosons and fermions from the production of Higgs bosons using the final state** (arXiv: 2205.05120)\n7. **Constraints on anomalous Higgs boson couplings to vector bosons and fermions using the final state in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV** (arXiv: 2605.14245)\n8. **Differential cross section measurements for the production of top quark pairs and of additional jets using dilepton events from $pp$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV** (arXiv: 2402.08486)\n9. **Effective field theory interpretation of ATLAS measurements involving the Higgs boson, electroweak bosons and the top quark** (arXiv: 2604.21670)\n\nThese analyses define various aspects of the lepton (electron or muon) ob