{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-1a53e034", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define a region requiring b-tagged jet?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses define regions that require b-tagged jets:\n\n1. **\"Had\" region** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and H_T requirements to remove trigger-efficiency dependence on jet multiplicity.\n2. **$t\\bar{t}$ control region (CR$_{t\\bar{t}}$)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n3. **0-lepton channel signal region (SR)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n4. **0L, 0 S-jet category** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n5. **0L, 1 S-jet category** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n6. **0L, >=5 S-jet category (inclusive)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n7. **1 b-tagged jet Signal Region (bsℓℓ / bbℓℓ)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n8. **1-lepton channel multi-jet control region (MJ-CR)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n9. **1-lepton channel signal region (SR)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n10. **12 non-overlapping signal regions categorized in N_H, N_jets, p_T^miss (Table 8)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n11. **1L, 0 S-jet category** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n12. **1L, 1 S-jet category** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n13. **2-lepton channel signal region (SR)** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n14. **2L, 0 S-jet category** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n15. **2ℓ SS Fiducial Region** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n16. **2ℓ SS Signal Region** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold, angular separation requirements, and a 2-jet or 3-jet category with at most one untagged jet in the 3-jet category.\n17. **2ℓ tt(e) HF non-prompt electron Control Regions** - This region includes a selection based on the MET trigger threshold and angular separation requirements.\n\nThese regions are", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "