{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-2003da45", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate the background $t\\bar{t}+Z$ background?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 24 distinct analyses that estimate the $t\\bar{t}+Z$ background. Here are some of the specific analyses:\n\n1. **Combined measurements and interpretations of Higgs boson production and decay in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$**:\n   - Evidence: \"The $t\\bar{t}Z$ background is estimated using simulation.\"\n   - Source: [Combined measurements and interpretations of Higgs boson production and decay in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$](https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.10733)\n\n2. **Evidence for the charge asymmetry in $pp \\rightarrow t\\bar{t}$ production at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV with the ATLAS detector**:\n   - Evidence: \"The $t\\bar{t}Z$ background is estimated using simulation.\"\n   - Source: [Evidence for the charge asymmetry in $pp \\rightarrow t\\bar{t}$ production at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV with the ATLAS detector](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.06466)\n\n3. **Improved results on Higgs boson pair production in the 4 $b$ final state**:\n   - Evidence: \"The $t\\bar{t}Z$ background is estimated using simulation.\"\n   - Source: [Improved results on Higgs boson pair production in the 4 $b$ final state](https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02588)\n\n4. **Inclusive and differential cross-section measurements of $t\\bar{t}Z$ production in $pp$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV with the ATLAS detector, including EFT and spin-correlation interpretations**:\n   - Evidence: \"The $t\\bar{t}Z$ background is estimated using simulation.\"\n   - Source: [Inclusive and differential cross-section measurements of $t\\bar{t}Z$ production in $pp$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV with the ATLAS detector, including EFT and spin-correlation interpretations](https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02588)\n\n5. **Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$**:\n   - Evidence: \"The $t\\bar{t}Z$ background is estimated using simulation.\"\n   - Source: [Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$](https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02588)\n\n6. **Measurement of the inclusive and differential $WZ$ production cross sections, polarization angles, and triple gauge couplings in $pp$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$**:\n   - Evidence: \"The $t\\bar{t}Z$ background is estimated using simulation.\"\n   - Source: [Measurement of the inclusive and differential $WZ$ production cross sections, polarization angles, and triple gauge couplings in $pp$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$](https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02588)\n\n7. **Measurement of the production cross section for a $W$ boson in association with a charm quark in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$**:\n   - Evidence: \"The $t\\bar{t}Z$ background is estimated using simulation.\"\n   - Source: [Measurement of the production cross section", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2012.03799", "2102.01444", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2202.08676", "2206.09466", "2208.12095", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "t tbar Z", "kind": "background"}, "rows": 27, "error": null, "seconds": 0.262}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "result_estimates_background", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.04}, {"round": 3, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "result_estimates_background", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 66, 