{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-27f0aed9", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses measured Relative charge asymmetry $A_{\\mathrm{C}}^{\\mathrm{rel}}$ vs $|\\Delta\\eta_{\\ell\\ell,\\,\\textrm{SS}}|$?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 18 distinct analyses that measured the relative charge asymmetry \\( A_{\\mathrm{C}}^{\\mathrm{rel}} \\) versus \\( |\\Delta\\eta_{\\ell\\ell, \\,\\textrm{SS}}| \\) or related observables.\n\nTo provide more context, here are some of the specific observables that were measured:\n\n- **Relative charge asymmetry \\( A_{\\mathrm{C}}^{\\mathrm{rel}} \\) vs \\( |\\Delta\\eta_{\\ell\\ell, \\,\\textrm{SS}}| \\)**: This is the primary observable you asked about.\n- **Differential cross section ratio \\( R_c^± \\) vs \\( |η^l| \\)**: Another related observable.\n- **Normalised differential \\( t\\bar{t}W \\) cross-section vs \\( |\\Delta\\eta_{\\ell\\ell, \\,\\textrm{SS}}| \\)**: This is a normalized version of the differential cross section.\n- **Absolute differential \\( t\\bar{t}W \\) cross-section vs \\( |\\Delta\\eta_{\\ell\\ell, \\,\\textrm{SS}}| \\)**: This is the absolute version of the differential cross section.\n\nThese measurements are spread across 18 distinct papers, with a total of 64 facts and 73 assertions recorded in the graph.\n\nIf you need more detailed information about specific papers or additional observables, please let me know.\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2009.14537", "2012.08600", "2106.01676", "2110.11231", "2112.03161", "2207.12246", "2208.12095", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2404.06204", "2504.13081", "2506.13565", "2508.13900"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Relative cha