{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-2ed26660", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses report the systematic uncertainty PDF and alpha_S uncertainty?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 48 distinct analyses that report the systematic uncertainty related to PDF and alpha_S. Here are some of the specific analyses and the exact systematics they report:\n\n1. **Combination of searches for nonresonant Higgs boson pair production in proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV} \\)**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties, PDF and factorization/renormalization scale uncertainty.\n\n2. **Combined measurements and interpretations of Higgs boson production and decay in proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV} \\)**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties, PDF and factorization/renormalization scale uncertainty, PDF and QCD scale (factorization/renormalization) theoretical uncertainty.\n\n3. **Constraints on anomalous Higgs boson couplings to vector bosons and fermions from the production of Higgs bosons using the final state**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n4. **Constraints on anomalous Higgs boson couplings to vector bosons and fermions using the final state in proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV} \\)**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n5. **Differential cross section measurements for the production of top quark pairs and of additional jets using dilepton events from \\( pp \\) collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV} \\)**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n6. **Effective field theory interpretation of ATLAS measurements involving the Higgs boson, electroweak bosons and the top quark**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n7. **Evidence for Higgs boson decay to a pair of muons**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n8. **Evidence for the charge asymmetry in \\( pp \\rightarrow t\\bar{t} \\) production at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13 \\) TeV with the ATLAS detector**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n9. **Fiducial WZ production cross section measurement (combined flavour categories)**:\n   - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n10. **General search for supersymmetric particles in scenarios with compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV} \\)**:\n    - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n11. **Improved results on Higgs boson pair production in the 4 \\( b \\) final state**:\n    - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n12. **Inclusive and differential cross section measurements of \\( t\\bar{t}b\\bar{b} \\) production in the lepton+jets channel at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV} \\)**:\n    - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\n13. **Inclusive and differential cross-section measurements of \\( t\\bar{t}Z \\) production in \\( pp \\) collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13 \\) TeV with the ATLAS detector, including EFT and spin-correlation interpretations**:\n    - Systematics: PDF and alpha_S uncertainty, PDF and scale uncertainties.\n\nThese analyses cover a wide range of topics, including Higgs boson pair production, top quark pair production, and various other processes", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2009.04363", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676"