{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-2f38a43b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define the region Control region CR^Z_VV for multi-boson background normalisation (3ℓ selection)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The analysis that defines the region \"Control region CR^Z_VV for multi-boson background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\" is found in the paper titled \"Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$\" (arXiv: 2202.08676).\n\nThis region is used for the normalisation of the multi-boson background in the 3-lepton selection.\n\nAnswer supported by the following assertion:\n- \"Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$\" defines the region \"3ℓ VV Control Region\" (assertion ID: hepkg:assertion:78dc38dbfdb2cad4b10a62ee).\n\nTherefore, the analysis that defines this region is reported in the paper \"Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$\".\n\nAnswer: The analysis defining the region \"Control region CR^Z_VV for multi-boson background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\" is found in the paper \"Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$\" (arXiv: 2202.08676).\n\nAnswerable: True\nReason: answered", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.14060", "2007.02873", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2012.01581", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2302.05225", "2304.08962", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2407.10549", "2408.03744", "2508.13900", "2510.07527", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "C