{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-30d66a63", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses measured Resolved Higgs boson coupling modifier (kappa_j)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses measured the Resolved Higgs boson coupling modifier (kappa_j):\n\n- **2001.06899**: Measurement of the associated production of a \\( \\mathup{{Z}} \\) boson with charm or bottom quark jets in proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13 \\) TeV.\n- **2009.04363**: Evidence for Higgs boson decay to a pair of muons.\n- **2111.08340**: Constraints on Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum using \\( H \\rightarrow b\\bar{b} \\) decays in the ATLAS detector.\n- **2504.13081**: Combination and interpretation of differential Higgs boson production cross sections in proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13 \\, \\text{TeV} \\).\n- **2602.18611**: Inclusive Higgs boson signal strength measurement.\n- **2602.18611**: Effective coupling modifier fit assuming no additional BSM decays.\n- **2602.18611**: Coupling modifier ratio fit.\n- **2602.18611**: Higgs boson trilinear self-coupling constraint via NLO EW corrections.\n- **2604.21670**: Effective field theory interpretation of ATLAS measurements involving the Higgs boson, electroweak bosons, and the top quark.\n- **2604.27044**: Combined Run 3 resolved+merged HH->4b result.\n- **2604.27044**: Combined Run 2 + Run 3 HH->4b result.\n\nThese analyses cover a range of topics, including Higgs boson production, decay, and coupling modifiers. Each analysis provides insights into different aspects of the Higgs boson's properties and interactions.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2009.04363", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2201.11585", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2207.12246", "2302.05225", "2407.1054