{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-58c34745", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define the region Validation region VR^Z_1F for fake/non-prompt lepton background?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The analysis that defines the region \"VR-$e\\mu$-fake validation region\" for the fake/non-prompt lepton background is found in the paper titled \"Search for chargino–neutralino pair production in final states with three leptons and missing transverse momentum in $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV $pp$ collisions with the ATLAS detector\" (arXiv: 2106.01676).\n\nThis region is characterized by:\n- An intermediate $E_T^{\\text{miss}}$ range, orthogonal to signal regions (SRs).\n- A lower bound on $m_{3l}$ to reduce WZ contamination.\n\nThese details are supported by the following quotes from the paper:\n- \"intermediate $E_T^{\\text{miss}}$ range, orthogonal to SRs\"\n- \"$m_{3l}$ lower bound to reduce WZ contamination\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis in question is part of the study described in the paper with arXiv ID 2106.01676.\n\nAnswer: The analysis defining the region \"VR-$e\\mu$-fake validation region\" for the fake/non-prompt lepton background is found in the paper \"Search for chargino–neutralino pair production in final states with three leptons and missing transverse momentum in $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV $pp$ collisions with the ATLAS detector\" (arXiv: 2106.01676).\n\nThis answer is based on the information retrieved from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2102.01444", "2106.01676", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2201.11585", "2206.09466", "2302.05225", "2304.08962", "2403.01556", "2404.06204", "2408.03744", "2506.13565", "2509.22535", "2602.18611", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Validation region VR^Z_1F", "kind": "event_region"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.362}, {"round": 2, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "result_defines_region", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 45, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}, {"round": 3, "tool": "describe", "args": {"entity_ids": ["hepkg:region:vr-ff-onshell"], "predicate": "region_has_selection"}, "rows": 2, "error": null, "seconds": 0.005}, {"round": 4, "tool": "papers_of", "args": {"entity_ids": ["hepkg:result:145b646dbebeacbefd96614b"]}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.01}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:region:SR_ttZ_Zbb", "hepkg:region:SR_ttZ_Zcc", "hepkg:region:VRL", "hepkg:region:VRS", "hepkg:region:VR_control_like", "hepkg:region:VR_sideband", "hepkg:region:VR_signal_like", "hepkg:region:background_validation_cr", "hepkg:region:control_region", "hepkg:region:cr-wz-offwz", "hepkg:region:cr-zz", "hepkg:region:cr_zee", "hepkg:region:cr_zmumu", "hepkg:region:cr_ztautau_nonvbf_ltau_lprime", "hepkg:region:cr_ztautau_vbf_ltau_lprime", "hepkg:region:hzz4l_vbf", "hepkg:region:merged1-VBF-VR", "hepkg:region:merged1-VR", "hepkg:region:qcd_mf_validation", "hepkg:region:res1-SR3b-ggHH", "hepkg:region:res2-SR-3MnT", "hepkg:region:sr-wz", "hepkg:region:ttbar-vr", "hepkg:region:validation-region-mll70to105", "hepkg:region:vbf-df-cr", "hepkg:region:vbf-sr", "hepkg:region:vbf_sr", "hepkg:region:vbf_top_cr", "hepkg:region:vbf_ztautau_cr", "hepkg:region:vr-0l-dphi", "hepkg:region:vr-0l-metsig", "hepkg:region:vr-2body-ttbar-df", "hepkg:region:vr-2body-ttbar-sf", "hepkg:region:vr-2body-ttbarZ", "hepkg:region:vr-3body-vv", "hepkg:region:vr-4body-ttbar", "hepkg:region:vr-4body-vv", "hepkg:region:vr-4body-vv-3l", "hepkg:region:vr-ee-fake", "hepkg:region:vr-ee-heavy-flavor", "hepkg:region:vr-emu-fake", "hepkg:region:vr-emu-heavy-flavor", "hepkg:region:vr-ff-offwz", "hepkg:region:vr-ff-onshell", "hepkg:region:vr-flavor-aligned-agnostic", "hepkg:region:vr-flavor-aligned-ml", "hepk