ght/loose lepton method)\".\n\n8. **$Z/\\gamma^{*}+\\text{jets}$ background** (`hepkg:background:zjets`):\n   - Uses methods such as \"Data-driven fake-factor/matrix method for FNP lepton estimation (tight/loose lepton method)\".\n\n9. **$t\\bar{t}$ background** (`hepkg:background:ttbar`):\n   - Uses methods such as \"Data-driven fake-factor/matrix method for FNP lepton estimation (tight/loose lepton method)\".\n\n10. **$t\\bar{t}+Z$ background** (`hepkg:background:ttbarZ`):\n    - Uses methods such as \"Data-driven fake-factor/matrix method for FNP lepton estimation (tight/loose lepton method)\".\n\n11. **Background from jets misidentified as tau_h candidates** (`hepkg:background:jet-to-tauh-misid`):\n    - Uses methods such as \"Data-driven fake-factor/matrix method for FNP lepton estimation (tight/loose lepton method)\".\n\n12. **Charge-flip electron background** (`hepkg:background:charge-flip-electrons`):\n    - Uses methods such as \"Data-driven fake-factor/matrix method for FNP lepton estimation (tight/loose lepton method)\".\n\nThese are just a few examples. The full list includes 113 distinct facts and 117 assertions across 44 distinct analyses.\n\nTo provide the exact papers, I will now list the papers that use these methods.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"papers_of\", \"arguments\": {\"entity_ids\": [\"hepkg:background:others-minor\", \"hepkg:background:diboson-vv\", \"hepkg:background:vgamma\", \"hepkg", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2404.06204", "2408.03744", "2