{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-8483efb4", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Data-driven fake-muon control-region method?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 44 distinct analyses that estimate a background using a method related to the \"Data-driven fake-muon control-region method.\"\n\nTo provide more context, here are the specific methods that were found:\n\n- Data-driven fake-muon control-region method\n- Data-driven lepton misidentification (fake-rate) method with OS/SS control regions\n- Data-driven same-sign (SS) control-region scale-factor method (dilepton fake-lepton estimate)\n- Data-driven matrix method (single-lepton channel fake-lepton estimate)\n- Z+X data-driven estimate using control region and lepton misidentification probabilities\n- Data-driven fake-factor/matrix method for FNP lepton estimation (tight/loose lepton method)\n- Data-driven fake-rate method using multijet control regions\n- Data-driven misidentified-lepton estimate using anti-identified control sample\n- Data-embedding technique (muon replacement)\n- Tight-to-loose data-driven nonprompt-lepton estimation method\n- Data-driven transfer-factor method for misidentified-lepton background (ltau_lprime, MC-template channel, OS/SS ratio)\n- Data-driven cosmic-ray background estimation using R_good ratio of cosmic-tagged muon quality\n- Data-driven electron charge mis-identification probability method\n- Data-driven misidentified-lepton estimate: prompt-lepton-subtracted SS \\( e\\mu \\) sample scaled by OS/SS ratio from simulation\n- Data-driven non-prompt lepton estimate via extrapolation factors\n- Control-region data-driven normalization\n- Data-driven eμ control-region method for top background\n- Data-driven fake-factor method\n- Data-driven \\( t\\bar{t} \\) estimation from \\( e\\mu \\) events\n- Background yield taken directly from MC simulation without data-driven correction\n- Fake-factor method using Id/anti-Id lepton definitions\n- MC simulation normalised to data in dedicated control regions (partially data-driven)\n- Data-driven multi-jet-enriched control-region template-fit method\n- Z boson mass peak control region data/simulation comparison\n- Fake-Factor method using a dedicated Z+jets control region (Symmetry method, F_FF component)\n\nThese methods are used across 44 distinct analyses.\n\nAnswer: **44 distinct analyses** estimate a background using a method related to the \"Data-driven fake-muon control-region method.\"", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2604.21670", "2604.27044", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Data-driven fake-muon control-region method", "kind": "background_method"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.365}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "background_uses_method", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.051}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:background_method:abcd_data_driven_crs", "hepkg:background_method:data_driven_fake_factor", "hepkg:background_method:data_driven_nonprompt_control_sample", "hepkg:background_method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:method:abcd-method", "hepkg:method:abcd-reweighting", "hepkg:method:charge_misid_data_driven",