{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-86ada70a", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define a region requiring Hadronically decaying tau lepton candidate (tau_h)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses define regions requiring a hadronically decaying tau lepton candidate (tau_h):\n\n- **2004.04545**: Defines the \"Lep\" and \"Had\" regions.\n- **2007.02873**: Defines the 1-lepton channel signal region (SR), 2-lepton channel signal region (SR), and 2-lepton channel eμ top control region (eμ-CR).\n- **2106.14246**: Defines the 2ℓSS search regions (SS01–SS20).\n- **2111.08340**: Defines the $t\\bar{t}$ control region (CR$_{t\\bar{t}}$).\n- **2202.08676**: Defines the 2L2T, 2L1T, 1L3T, and 1L2T channels.\n- **2312.04450**: Defines the 2ℓ-eμ-5j2b (data-driven ttbar control region).\n- **2401.05299**: Defines the 2ℓ SS Signal Region, 2ℓ SS Fiducial Region, 2ℓ tt(e) HF non-prompt electron Control Regions, and 2ℓ tt(μ) HF non-prompt muon Control Regions.\n- **2508.13900**: Defines the 0L, ≥5 S-jet category (inclusive), 1L, 0 S-jet category, and 2L, 0 S-jet category.\n\nThese regions and channels are part of the analyses reported in these papers.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2207.12246", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2404.06204", "2405.1866