{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-bfad537a", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses measured H -> tau tau?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 21 distinct analyses that measured the H -> tau tau process.\n\nTo provide more context, let's list the specific processes that were targeted:\n\n- H -> tau tau decay (Higgs decay to a pair of leptons)\n- HH -> bb tau tau -> bb l l nu nu nu nu (dilepton)\n- H -> e tau (lepton-flavour-violating Higgs decay)\n- $H \\rightarrow \\mu \\tau$\n- H -> bb\n- ttH(H->bb)\n- H -> diphoton\n- H -> WW\n- H -> gammagamma\n- H → ZZ → 4ℓ\n- ttH(H->cc)\n- H → Za (a → hadrons)\n- H → Z η_c\n- Neutral-current high-mass Drell-Yan (Z/gamma* -> tau tau)\n- HH -> bb ZZ* (minor contribution, included in acceptance)\n- HH -> bb WW* -> bb l l nu nu (dilepton)\n- gg → H\n- pp -> Z' -> Hγ, H -> b b̄\n- H → μ+μ−\n- H(inv)\n- $Z(\\to\\tau\\tau)$+jets background\n- gg -> H + 2 jets\n- VH(H->cc)\n- X -> HH\n- $t\\overline{t}H$\n\nHowever, the primary focus is on the H -> tau tau decay, which is the most relevant process for your question.\n\nWould you like more details on any specific analysis or process?", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2503.19420", "2504.13081", "2509.22535", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "H -> tau tau", "kind": "physics_process"}, "rows": 29, "error": null, "seconds": 0.276}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "result_targets_process", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.025}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:proce