{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-c4d34f1b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate the background Combinatorial background?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses estimate the combinatorial background:\n\n1. **2602.18611** - Combined measurements and interpretations of Higgs boson production and decay in proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV} \\)\n2. **2111.08340** - Constraints on Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum using \\( H \\rightarrow b\\bar{b} \\) decays in the ATLAS detector\n3. **2205.05120** - Constraints on anomalous Higgs boson couplings to vector bosons and fermions from the production of Higgs bosons using the \\( b\\bar{b}\\tau\\tau \\) final state\n4. **2208.12095** - Evidence for the charge asymmetry in \\( pp \\rightarrow t\\bar{t} \\) production at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13 \\) TeV with the ATLAS detector\n5. **2510.07527** - HH→WWγγ analysis result\n6. **2510.07527** - HH→γγττ analysis result\n7. **2604.27044** - Improved results on Higgs boson pair production in the 4 \\( b \\) final state\n8. **2312.04450** - Inclusive and differential cross-section measurements of \\( t\\bar{t}Z \\) production in \\( pp \\) collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s}=13 \\) TeV with the ATLAS detector, including EFT and spin-correlation interpretations\n\nThese analyses cover a range of topics, including Higgs boson production, top quark production, and diboson production, among others. Each of these analyses explicitly estimates the combinatorial background as part of their methodology.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2102.01444", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2205.05120",