{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-e37e8481", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Background normalization and shape determined via direct fit to data using parametric functions?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 44 analyses that estimate a background using the method \"Background normalization and shape determined via direct fit to data using parametric functions\" or similar methods. \n\nTo provide more context, here are some of the specific methods used:\n\n- **Control-region-based background normalisation via simultaneous profile likelihood fit**\n- **Direct MC simulation and theoretical cross-section prediction**\n- **Data-driven normalisation via simultaneous profile-likelihood fit in dedicated control regions**\n- **Direct MC simulation estimate (no control-region normalisation)**\n- **Data-driven fake-factor method**\n\nThese methods are used across various backgrounds, including $t\\bar{t}$, $W$+jets, $Z$+jets, and others.\n\nIf you need more detailed information on specific analyses or backgrounds, please let me know.\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2604.27044", "2605.1