{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-f264eb8b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses used the generator POWHEG-BOX-RES?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses used the generator POWHEG-BOX-RES or related versions:\n\n- **2004.01678**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ background MC sample.\n- **2004.14060**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ background MC sample.\n- **2006.05880**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ MC sample.\n- **2009.04363**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ background MC sample.\n- **2102.01444**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ MC sample.\n- **2107.12553**: Used simulated SM $t\\bar{t}$ sample.\n- **2109.13808**: Used single-top $Wt$ production sample.\n- **2202.08676**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ MC simulation sample.\n- **2303.15340**: Used various $t\\bar{t}$ samples including ISR variations, reweighting, and different configurations.\n- **2307.01094**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ simulated sample.\n- **2407.10549**: Used $Vh$ associated production background sample.\n- **2408.03744**: Used $t\\bar{t}$ MC samples.\n- **2503.19420**: Used $q\\bar{q} \\to WH$, $q\\bar{q} \\to ZH$, and $gg \\to ZH$ simulated samples.\n\nThese analyses collectively cover a range of processes and configurations, demonstrating the versatility and widespread use of POWHEG-BOX-RES in high-energy physics research.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The following analyses used the generator POWHEG-BOX-RES or related versions:\\n\\n- **2004.01678**: Used $t\\\\bar{t}$ background MC sample.\\n- **2004.14060**: Used $t\\\\bar{t}$ background MC sample.\\n- **2006.05880**: Used $t\\\\bar{t}$ MC sample.\\n- **2009.04363**: Used $t\\\\bar{t}$ background MC sample.\\n- **2102.01444**: Used $t\\\\bar{t}$ MC sample.\\n- **2107.12553**: Used simulated SM $t\\\\bar{t}$ sample.\\n- **2109.13808**: Used single-top $Wt$ production sample.\\n- **2202.08676**: Used $t\\\\