{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48229", "qid": "gen-retrieval-f3ae73c6", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate the background FNP lepton background (ttbar, tW, WW, Z+jets) in RJR selection?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph indicates that the following analyses estimate the FNP lepton background (ttbar, tW, WW, Z+jets) in the RJR selection:\n\n1. **HH->bbWW, WW->lvqq/2l2nu analysis** (Paper: [2510.07527](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07527))\n2. **HH->multilepton analysis** (Paper: [2510.07527](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07527))\n3. **Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena** (Paper: [2202.08676](https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.08676))\n\nHowever, the graph does not provide specific details on which analyses estimate the FNP lepton background in the RJR low-mass signal region (SR3l-Low) or the RJR ISR signal region (SR3l-ISR). The comparisons for these specific regions show no shared or unique results.\n\nTherefore, based on the available data, the analyses that estimate the FNP lepton background in the RJR selection are found in the papers [2510.07527](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07527) and [2202.08676](https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.08676).\n\nAnswering your question:\n- **Papers**: [2510.07527](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07527) and [2202.08676](https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.08676)\n- **Analyses**: HH->bbWW, WW->lvqq/2l2nu, HH->multilepton, and Inclusive nonresonant multilepton probes of new phenomena.\n\nThe graph does not specify the exact regions (SR3l-Low or SR3l-ISR) for these estimates.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111